	"dialog.gestures.warning_msg": "⚠️ Warning: Enabling trackpad gestures may interfere with system gestures.\n\nTo avoid conflicts, disable the following macOS options:\n\n• 2-finger trackpad gestures: disable scroll and swipe if you want to use them in Hammerspoon.\n• 3-finger trackpad gestures to move windows and select text\n• 3-finger tap to look up words in the dictionary\n• 3-finger horizontal/vertical swipe to switch spaces, activate App Exposé or Mission Control\n• 4-finger horizontal/vertical swipe to switch spaces, activate App Exposé or Mission Control\n\nIt is important to disable 4-finger system gestures in order to define 5-finger gestures. Otherwise, macOS would not distinguish between them and would prevent 5-finger gestures from working. That is why the default 4-finger gestures are redefined in the Gestures module to restore system functions without conflict with 5-finger gestures.",
